## Operators

### Theory: Operator Categories

Operators are symbols that perform operations on values:

```
1. Arithmetic: +, -, *, /, %, **
2. Comparison: ==, ===, !=, !==, <, >, <=, >=, <=>
3. Logical: &&, ||, !, and, or, xor
4. Assignment: =, +=, -=, *=, /=, %=, .=
5. String: . (concatenation)
6. Array: + (union), == (equal), === (identical)
7. Ternary: ? :
8. Null coalescing: ??
9. Spaceship: <=> (comparison)
10. Error: @
```

### Arithmetic Operators

```php
<?php
$a = 10;
$b = 3;

echo $a + $b;               // 13 (addition)
echo $a - $b;               // 7 (subtraction)
echo $a * $b;               // 30 (multiplication)
echo $a / $b;               // 3.3333... (division)
echo $a % $b;               // 1 (modulo)
echo $a ** $b;              // 1000 (exponentiation)
echo -$a;                   // -10 (unary minus)

// Increment/Decrement
$x = 5;
echo ++$x;                  // 6 (pre-increment)
echo $x++;                  // 6 (post-increment, then x becomes 7)
echo $x;                    // 7
?>
```

### Comparison Operators

```php
<?php
// Loose comparison (==) - coerces types
0 == false;                 // true
"0" == false;               // true
"" == false;                // true
1 == true;                  // true
"1" == true;                // true

// Strict comparison (===) - no type coercion
0 === false;                // false
"0" === false;              // false
1 === true;                 // false

// Spaceship operator (<=>)
1 <=> 2;                    // -1 (less than)
2 <=> 2;                    // 0 (equal)
3 <=> 2;                    // 1 (greater than)

// Null safe operator (?->)
$user = null;
$name = $user?->getName();  // Returns null (no error)
?>
```

### Logical Operators

```php
<?php
$x = true;
$y = false;

$x && $y;                   // false (AND)
$x || $y;                   // true (OR)
!$x;                        // false (NOT)

// Difference: && vs and, || vs or
($x = true) && ($y = false);   // && has higher precedence
$x = true && $y = false;       // $x = (true && false) = false

$x = true and $y = false;      // 'and' has lower precedence
$x = (true and $y = false);    // Different!
?>
```

### String Operator

```php
<?php
$str1 = "Hello";
$str2 = "World";

$result = $str1 . " " . $str2;  // "Hello World"

// String concatenation assignment
$str1 .= "!";                   // $str1 = "Hello!"

// String access (like array)
$str = "Hello";
echo $str[0];                   // "H"
echo $str[-1];                  // "o" (last character)
$str[0] = "J";                  // $str = "Jello"
?>
```

### Null Coalescing Operator

```php
<?php
// ?? - returns first defined non-null value
$name = $user['name'] ?? 'Guest';

// Null coalescing assignment (PHP 7.4+)
$name ??= 'Guest';              // If $name is null, set to 'Guest'

// Chaining
$value = $a ?? $b ?? $c ?? 'default';

// Comparison to ternary
$x = isset($y) ? $y : 'default';
$x = $y ?? 'default';           // Shorter, same result
?>
```

