## Arrays

### Theory: PHP Arrays

PHP arrays are **ordered maps** (associative arrays):
- Key-value pairs
- Keys can be strings or integers
- Maintain insertion order
- Foundation of many PHP structures

```php
<?php
// Indexed array (integer keys, auto-assigned)
$arr1 = ["a", "b", "c"];        // Keys: 0, 1, 2

// Associative array (string keys)
$arr2 = ["name" => "John", "age" => 30];

// Mixed keys
$arr3 = [0 => "zero", "key" => "value", 1 => "one"];
?>
```

### Array Operations

```php
<?php
// Creation
$arr = [];                      // Empty array
$arr = array();                 // Old syntax
$arr = array_fill(0, 5, 0);    // Fill with value
$arr = range(1, 10);            // 1 to 10
$arr = array_combine($keys, $values);

// Access
$arr = ["a", "b", "c"];
echo $arr[0];                   // "a"
$arr[1] = "B";                  // Modify
$arr[] = "d";                   // Append (next index)

// Checking
isset($arr[0]);                 // true if exists
isset($arr[10]);                // false if out of range
array_key_exists(0, $arr);      // More explicit
empty($arr);                    // true if empty

// Iteration
foreach ($arr as $value) {
    echo $value;
}

foreach ($arr as $key => $value) {
    echo "$key => $value";
}
?>
```

### Useful Array Functions

```php
<?php
$arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

// Counting
count($arr);                    // 5
sizeof($arr);                   // 5 (alias)

// Searching
in_array(3, $arr);              // true
array_search(3, $arr);          // 2 (key)
array_key_exists("name", $assoc);

// Modification
array_push($arr, 6);            // Add to end
array_pop($arr);                // Remove from end
array_unshift($arr, 0);         // Add to beginning
array_shift($arr);              // Remove from beginning

// Merging
$merged = array_merge($arr1, $arr2);
$merged = $arr1 + $arr2;        // Union

// Filtering & Mapping
$even = array_filter($arr, fn($x) => $x % 2 == 0);
$doubled = array_map(fn($x) => $x * 2, $arr);

// Reducing
$sum = array_reduce($arr, fn($carry, $item) => $carry + $item, 0);

// Sorting
sort($arr);                     // Ascending
rsort($arr);                    // Descending
asort($arr);                    // Keep keys
ksort($arr);                    // Sort by key
usort($arr, fn($a, $b) => $b - $a);  // Custom sort
?>
```

