## Database Basics

### Theory: Databases in Web Development

Databases store persistent data:
- **Relational**: MySQL, PostgreSQL (tables, rows, columns)
- **NoSQL**: MongoDB, Redis (documents, key-value)
- **PHP Integration**: PDO (recommended), MySQLi

### PDO (PHP Data Objects)

```php
<?php
// Connection
$dsn = "mysql:host=localhost;dbname=mydb";
$pdo = new PDO($dsn, "root", "password");

// Query (SELECT)
$stmt = $pdo->query("SELECT * FROM users");
$users = $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
foreach ($users as $user) {
    echo $user['name'];
}

// Fetch single row
$stmt = $pdo->query("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 1");
$user = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);

// Prepared statements (prevent SQL injection)
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?");
$stmt->execute(["user@example.com"]);
$user = $stmt->fetch();

// Named placeholders
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (:name, :email)");
$stmt->execute([
    ":name" => "John",
    ":email" => "john@example.com"
]);

// Get last insert ID
$id = $pdo->lastInsertId();

// Update
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("UPDATE users SET name = ? WHERE id = ?");
$stmt->execute(["New Name", 1]);

// Delete
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("DELETE FROM users WHERE id = ?");
$stmt->execute([1]);

// Error handling
try {
    $pdo->query("SELECT * FROM nonexistent");
} catch (PDOException $e) {
    echo "Error: " . $e->getMessage();
}
?>
```

