### Scenario 1: Performance Issue

```php
<?php
// Problem: Dashboard loads in 5 seconds

// Step 1: Profile the code
// Use: Xdebug, Blackfire, New Relic

// Step 2: Identify bottleneck
// Result: Database queries taking 4 seconds

// Step 3: Analyze queries
$users = User::with(['posts', 'comments'])  // Eager load
    ->where('active', true)
    ->limit(100)
    ->get();

// Step 4: Add caching
$users = Cache::remember('active_users_list', 3600, function() {
    return User::with(['posts', 'comments'])
        ->where('active', true)
        ->limit(100)
        ->get();
});

// Step 5: Monitor
// Result: Dashboard now loads in 200ms

// Step 6: Invalidate cache on updates
public function updateUser(User $user, array $data) {
    $user->update($data);
    Cache::forget('active_users_list');
}
?>
```

### Scenario 2: Data Consistency Issue

```php
<?php
// Problem: Order totals don't match invoice amounts

// Root cause analysis
// 1. Race condition in concurrent updates
// 2. No transaction wrapping

// Solution: Use database transactions
DB::transaction(function() {
    $order = Order::lockForUpdate()->find($orderId);
    
    $order->items()->each(function($item) {
        // Update with lock
        $item->increment('quantity');
    });
    
    // Recalculate total atomically
    $order->calculateTotal();
    $order->save();
});

// Prevent race condition
// All database queries within transaction execute atomically
?>
```

