## Common Mistakes & How to Avoid Them

```php
<?php
// Mistake 1: Not validating input
❌ $email = $_POST['email'];
✅ $email = request()->validate(['email' => 'required|email']);

// Mistake 2: Direct SQL queries (SQL injection)
❌ "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = " . $id;
✅ DB::prepared("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?", [$id]);

// Mistake 3: No error handling
❌ $data = json_decode($response);
✅ $data = json_decode($response, true);
   if (json_last_error() !== JSON_ERROR_NONE) {
       throw new Exception('Invalid JSON');
   }

// Mistake 4: Not using transactions for related operations
❌ $user->save();
   $user->roles()->attach($role);  // Might fail!
   
✅ DB::transaction(function() use ($user, $role) {
       $user->save();
       $user->roles()->attach($role);
   });

// Mistake 5: Hardcoding configuration
❌ $db_host = 'localhost';
✅ $db_host = config('database.host');  // From .env

// Mistake 6: Not testing edge cases
❌ function divide($a, $b) { return $a / $b; }
✅ function divide($a, $b) {
       if ($b == 0) throw new DivisionByZeroException();
       return $a / $b;
   }

// Mistake 7: Ignoring performance
❌ foreach ($users as $user) { echo count($user->posts); }
✅ $users = User::with('posts')->get();
   foreach ($users as $user) { echo $user->posts->count(); }

// Mistake 8: Not logging errors
❌ try { ... } catch (Exception $e) { /* silent fail */ }
✅ try { ... } catch (Exception $e) {
       Log::error('Failed to process', ['error' => $e]);
       throw $e;
   }
?>
