**Theory:** Encapsulation protects internal state:
- `public` - accessible everywhere
- `protected` - accessible in class and subclasses
- `private` - accessible only in same class
- Enables validation and control

### Type Covariance & Contravariance (PHP 7.4+)

```php
<?php
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}

interface Repository {
    public function find($id): Animal;  // Return type covariant
}

class DogRepository implements Repository {
    // Returning Dog (subtype of Animal) is allowed (covariance)
    public function find($id): Dog {
        return new Dog();
