## Type System Deep Dive

### Type Declarations & Strict Mode

```php
<?php
// Without type declarations (loose)
function add($a, $b) {
    return $a + $b;
}
add(2, 3);                  // 5
add("2", "3");              // 5 (coerced)
add("2 apples", "3");       // 2 (coerced, 2 + 0)

// With type declarations (PHP 7+)
function addStrict(int $a, int $b): int {
    return $a + $b;
}
addStrict(2, 3);            // 5
addStrict("2", "3");        // 5 (coerced to int by default)
// addStrict("2 apples", 3); // TypeError! Coercion fails

// Strict mode - NO coercion
declare(strict_types=1);

function addVeryStrict(int $a, int $b): int {
    return $a + $b;
}
addVeryStrict(2, 3);        // 5
// addVeryStrict("2", 3);   // TypeError! Must be int
// addVeryStrict(2.5, 3);   // TypeError! No float to int coercion

// Nullable types
function getName(?string $name): ?string {
    return $name ?? 'Unknown';
}
getName('John');            // 'John'
getName(null);              // 'Unknown'

// Union types (PHP 8+)
function process(int|float $value): int|float {
    return $value * 2;
}
process(5);                 // 10
process(5.5);               // 11

// Mixed type (PHP 8+)
function flexible(mixed $value): mixed {
    return $value;
}

// Void return type
function log(string $message): void {
    echo $message;
    // No return statement needed
}

// Never type (PHP 8.1+) - function never returns
function throw_error(): never {
    throw new Exception("Error!");
}
?>
```

**Type System Concepts:**
- **Strong typing**: All types checked strictly
- **Weak typing**: Types coerced when possible
- **Static typing**: Types checked at compile time
- **Dynamic typing**: Types checked at runtime
- **Type hints**: Optional declarations
- **Type inference**: Automatic type deduction

