### Generators (Memory Efficient)

```php
<?php
// Problem: Reading large file uses lots of memory
// Bad approach - loads everything
$lines = [];
foreach (file('large-file.txt') as $line) {
    $lines[] = $line;
}
// All lines in memory!

// Good approach - generator yields one at a time
function readFile($filename) {
    $fp = fopen($filename, 'r');
    try {
        while (!feof($fp)) {
            yield fgets($fp);
        }
    } finally {
        fclose($fp);
    }
}

foreach (readFile('large-file.txt') as $line) {
    echo $line;  // One line at a time!
}

// Generator with keys
function generateRange($start, $end) {
    for ($i = $start; $i <= $end; $i++) {
        yield $i => "Item $i";
    }
}

foreach (generateRange(1, 3) as $key => $value) {
    echo "$key: $value\n";
}

// Generator delegation
function generate1to3() {
    yield 1;
    yield 2;
    yield from generate4to6();  // Delegate
}

function generate4to6() {
    yield 4;
    yield 5;
    yield 6;
}

// Generator expression (PHP 7+)
$numbers = (function() {
    for ($i = 1; $i <= 3; $i++) {
        yield $i;
    }
})();

// Two-way communication with generator
function echoGen() {
    $value = yield;
    echo "Received: $value\n";
    yield;
}

$gen = echoGen();
$gen->next();                   // Start generator
$gen->send("Hello");            // Send value to generator
?>
```

**Benefits:**
- Memory efficient for large datasets
- Lazy evaluation
- Readable code for sequential processing

