### Q6: How do you handle file uploads securely?

**Answer:**
```php
<?php
// ❌ UNSAFE - No validation
move_uploaded_file($_FILES['photo']['tmp_name'], 'uploads/' . $_FILES['photo']['name']);
// Problems: Any file type, name collision, no size limit, public directory

// ✅ SAFE - Complete validation
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST') {
    $file = $_FILES['upload'] ?? null;
    
    // 1. Check upload errors
    if (!$file || $file['error'] !== UPLOAD_ERR_OK) {
        echo "Upload error: " . $file['error'];
        exit;
    }
    
    // 2. Check file size
    $max_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024;  // 5MB
    if ($file['size'] > $max_size) {
        echo "File too large";
        exit;
    }
    
    // 3. Validate MIME type (check actual file content, not extension)
    $finfo = finfo_open(FILEINFO_MIME_TYPE);
    $mime = finfo_file($finfo, $file['tmp_name']);
    finfo_close($finfo);
    
    $allowed_types = ['image/jpeg', 'image/png', 'image/gif'];
    if (!in_array($mime, $allowed_types)) {
        echo "Invalid file type: $mime";
        exit;
    }
    
    // 4. Validate image dimensions (for images)
    $image_info = getimagesize($file['tmp_name']);
    if (!$image_info || $image_info[0] > 4000 || $image_info[1] > 4000) {
        echo "Image dimensions invalid";
        exit;
    }
    
    // 5. Generate secure filename
    $extension = pathinfo($file['name'], PATHINFO_EXTENSION);
    $filename = bin2hex(random_bytes(16)) . '.' . strtolower($extension);
    
    // 6. Move to secure directory (outside web root)
    $upload_dir = '/var/uploads/';  // Not in web root!
    $filepath = $upload_dir . $filename;
    
    if (!move_uploaded_file($file['tmp_name'], $filepath)) {
        echo "Failed to save file";
        exit;
    }
    
    // 7. Store in database (not filesystem path)
    $db->prepare("INSERT INTO files (filename, original_name, mime_type) VALUES (?, ?, ?)")
       ->execute([$filename, $file['name'], $mime]);
    
    echo "File uploaded successfully";
}
?>
```

**Security Checklist:**
- ✓ Check `$_FILES['file']['error']`
- ✓ Validate file size
- ✓ Check MIME type (use `finfo`, not extension)
- ✓ Validate image dimensions
- ✓ Generate random filename
- ✓ Store outside web root
- ✓ Store filename in database
- ✓ Don't execute uploaded files
- ✓ Set proper directory permissions

