### Q9: How do you work with JSON in PHP?

**Answer:**
```php
<?php
// PHP array to JSON
$data = [
    'name' => 'John',
    'age' => 30,
    'emails' => ['john@example.com', 'john@work.com'],
    'active' => true
];

$json = json_encode($data);
// {"name":"John","age":30,"emails":["john@example.com","john@work.com"],"active":true}

// Encoding options
$pretty = json_encode($data, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT);
$unescaped = json_encode($data, JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES);
$numeric_keys = json_encode($data, JSON_FORCE_OBJECT);  // Array as object

// JSON to PHP array
$json_string = '{"name":"Alice","age":25,"verified":true}';
$array = json_decode($json_string, true);  // true = associative array
// ['name' => 'Alice', 'age' => 25, 'verified' => true]

// JSON to object (without true parameter)
$obj = json_decode($json_string);  // Returns stdClass
echo $obj->name;                   // "Alice"

// Error handling - CRITICAL!
$invalid_json = '{"invalid": json}';
$result = json_decode($invalid_json, true);

if (json_last_error() !== JSON_ERROR_NONE) {
    $error = json_last_error_msg();
    echo "JSON Error: $error";
}

// Working with files
$data = ['users' => [...], 'total' => 100];
file_put_contents('data.json', json_encode($data, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT));

$data = json_decode(file_get_contents('data.json'), true);

// Best practices
class JsonService {
    public static function encode($data): string {
        $json = json_encode($data);
        if (json_last_error() !== JSON_ERROR_NONE) {
            throw new JsonException(json_last_error_msg());
        }
        return $json;
    }
    
    public static function decode(string $json): array {
        $data = json_decode($json, true);
        if (json_last_error() !== JSON_ERROR_NONE) {
            throw new JsonException(json_last_error_msg());
        }
        return $data;
    }
}

// Usage
try {
    $json = JsonService::encode($data);
    $decoded = JsonService::decode($json);
} catch (JsonException $e) {
    // Handle error
}
?>
```

**Common Issues:**
- Forgetting to check `json_last_error()`
- Using stdClass instead of arrays
- Not handling large JSON files
- Encoding/decoding special characters

